--- MESSAGE ---
DomainLineOf is the first member of the transform domain

359e590 made GenDrake a domain of transform types with an empty list of them. a052883 put the
first substitution string on the target side. This is the member that joins the two: a definition
in, the target's line out.

    type DomainLineOf from draco draketarget DomainLine
      factory
        parameters
          par definition TypeDefinition
        body
          loc line DomainLine parameters
            par _definition.domainAspect.typeName.namePackage
            par _definition.domainAspect.typeName.name
          fix value String line.value
    domain draco gendrake GenDrake

It has the shape the scenario's gate 4 states for a transform member and the shape the old
gendrake.Emission had before it moved up: derives a type on the target side, takes a parameter typed
in the source, computes the target's value. Now that the source IS TypeDefinition (359e590), the
parameter's type and the domain's source line say the same word. Nothing in the body is Scala —
two path selections on the definition, one construction on the application surface, one read of
the target type's own value — so nothing needed declaring.

The test that was written as this member's oracle becomes exactly that. DomainLineTest's corpus
sweep built DomainLine from the pointer by hand; now it hands DomainLineOf the definition and
compares. The by-hand mapping is gone from the test tree, and the sweep grows by one line: the
member's own.

Authored through the parser again — .drake first, parse to .json, emit back exact — and this time
the engine needed no splice, since a052883's symbol table is in the compiled classes. GenDrake's
.json was edited by hand for its member list and confirmed identical to what parse gives.

WHAT IS NEXT. One line of a definition's surface is definition-backed end to end. The type header
is the next form, and it is the first with a CONDITIONAL clause — `from` appears only when a
derivation does — which is the first substitution string that needs more than `++` and `join`.

